<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1196–<a href="/years/1217">1217</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Baglers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bagler were a faction in the Norwegian civil wars, formed in 1196 by opponents of King Sverre with the backing of the church, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Nicholas Arnesson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>. Strongest in the east around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslofjord">Oslofjord</a>, they set up rival kings and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birkebeiner">Birkebeiner</a> for two decades. A settlement in 1208 and the accession of Haakon IV in 1217 brought the factions together.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagler.jpg" alt="Bagler" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Knud Bergslien · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birkebeinerne_ski01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
